1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Inga Marie writes - .
2 CONT
2 CONT In Kaldfarnes, my father was the village postmaster and express agent.  All shipping was by steamship that came four times a week  Our house was a gathering place to get and send mail. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He kept posted what went on in the world, and tried his hardest to get people to the voting place when there was an election.
2 CONT
2 CONT My father always read the text on Sundays using a book called Lars Linderot.  Sometimes the neighbors came when Dad had devotions, and he would sing from the hymn book just like we did in church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother and father were very strict with me.  Dad did not have to say a word, but that look in his eyes was worse than any words.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was a terrible shock when Mother told me Dad had bladder cancer.  I pleaded with the Lord to spare his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT At his bedside he said - whatever happens, take good care of your character.  You will never feel sorry.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was only 47.  It was December 16, 1903.  I was 16.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * 1856.8	 
2 CONT * 18.01.1856	 
2 CONT * 25.05.1856	 	 
2 CONT * Jørgen Christian	 
2 CONT * E	 
2 CONT * ind	Andreas	Carstensen	 
2 CONT * Øresvik	 
2 CONT * [Hjd] 
2 CONT * kone	Bergitta	Jensd	 
2 CONT
