2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Andreassen home 
2 NOTE This is the house that once was the Andreassen home, then taken apart and rebuilt farther in the fjord.
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p10/4966/3456/5344483814a79efc/Grandma_s_neighbor_s_house_i_Kaldfarnes_original.jpg?hash=68454eb77b248296c30bc42265eb1730c69e16cd0dbd5a02e149cc2c95014396.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Neighbor's house at Kaldfarnes
2 NOTE If you have been to Kaldfarnes, you have probably had your picture taken sitting on these big rocks just left of the pole.  They are referred to as Grandma's front porch.  The Andreassen house was here, next to the Andreas Nikolai
3 CONC sen home, during Inga's childhod.  At some time, it was taken apart and rebuilt farther in the fjord.  At Medby I think.
3 CONT In Inga's Story book, Grandma calls the neighbor lady Ellen and the children Evan, Conrad, Alma, and Clark.  In the Bygdebok the mother is Else Tollefsen, the children - Ingvard, Øyvind, Alma, and Klerk.  
3 CONT In 2001, some boards were off the window on the side of this house.  I coud see that Else' tablecloth was still on the table.
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p10/4966/3456/5344483814a79efd/Kaldfarnes_fra_Bygdebok_I_original.jpg?hash=9bb50272e90a5f33f5275cdb37e265a1289d8d5476b2509efca420a7bbc8ed4d.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Road to Kaldfarnes - Bygdebok I page 425
2 NOTE  In her Bygdebok I,  Grandma shows in this picture where their house was, their boat house, and the dock.
3 CONT
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p10/4966/3456/5344483814a79efe/Kaldfarnes_drawing_original.jpg?hash=724a81ea593ce8e5c5eae1d3d26f166d1757d387c8021f4517fe519c1eefeefe.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Old Kaldfarnes - Bygdebok II page 244
2 NOTE In her Bygdebok, Grandma has written on this picture,  "The house where I was born".  
3 CONT If I translated properly, this is a drawing how Kaldfarnes was in 1880.  Aron and Nikolay Andreassen where brothers.  Somewhere I read that Nikolay (also spelled Nikolai) sold this farm to Jens Wilsgaard.  Jens had married Dorthea
3 CONC  who was born and raised at Kalfarnes by parents Iver Hansen and Helene Eidisdatter.  Jens sold half the farm to Nikolai's son Andreas Nikolaisen.  The other half of the farm he gave to Margrethe only, as her inheritance.  In this
3 CONC  picture you can see the path from Grandma's house to the dock, also the boathouse where the boat would have to be pulled down to the water.  
3 CONT To our families in Norway - If you know more about this picture, would you please leave a comment.  Takk
