2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Road to Kaldfarnes - Bygdebok I page 425
2 NOTE  In her Bygdebok I,  Grandma shows in this picture where their house was, their boat house, and the dock.
3 CONT
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p10/4966/3456/5344483814a79efe/Kaldfarnes_drawing_original.jpg?hash=724a81ea593ce8e5c5eae1d3d26f166d1757d387c8021f4517fe519c1eefeefe.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Old Kaldfarnes - Bygdebok II page 244
2 NOTE In her Bygdebok, Grandma has written on this picture,  "The house where I was born".  
3 CONT If I translated properly, this is a drawing how Kaldfarnes was in 1880.  Aron and Nikolay Andreassen where brothers.  Somewhere I read that Nikolay (also spelled Nikolai) sold this farm to Jens Wilsgaard.  Jens had married Dorthea
3 CONC  who was born and raised at Kalfarnes by parents Iver Hansen and Helene Eidisdatter.  Jens sold half the farm to Nikolai's son Andreas Nikolaisen.  The other half of the farm he gave to Margrethe only, as her inheritance.  In this
3 CONC  picture you can see the path from Grandma's house to the dock, also the boathouse where the boat would have to be pulled down to the water.  
3 CONT To our families in Norway - If you know more about this picture, would you please leave a comment.  Takk
