2 TITL Torsken 1907
2 NOTE Thank you to Bjorn Antonsen and his mother in Skaland, for telling me what Iver has written to Margrethe on this postcard.
3 CONT Dear Sister.  Today I am traveling to see our King. He is in Harstad tomorrow.  We are well to this date.  Regards from your brother Iver Kongsnes.  July 29, 1907.
3 CONT When Margrethe and Inga Marie were on their way to the USA, they had a couple days in Trondheim.  Inga wrote on April 29, 1906 -  "We also went to see the old Cathedral.  That was something to see.  It was just getting ready for K
3 CONC ing Haakon to be crowned.  We wanted so badly to stay and see the coronation, but we just had to go on."
3 CONT So now we know the date is 1907
2 NOTE I thought this date was July 29, 1907, but maybe it is 1904.  I only have a copy, the original postcard is in your Mother's book.  Would be interesting to see what it says on the other side of the postcard.  Margrethe was in Troms
3 CONC ø in 1904. Olav wanted a copy of this postcard for his book too.  You can see what he did with it.  It is in his book on pages 332 and 333.  
2 NOTE I love this postcard!  Can visualize this very same scene from Olav's small boat coming across the fjord from our wonderful day at Kongsnes.  Are those numbers on the bottom the date... July 29th, 1904 ?  If so that would have bee
3 CONC n taken around 100 years before Brady and I visited.  Amazing!
2 NOTE To Margrethe in Silverton OR, from her brother Iver in Kongsnes on Senja.
