2 NOTE Inga says - "Freda's mother-in-law found out the house next to them was for sale.  Freda and Herb to me out to look at it.  It was an old house, but it had been kept up well."
3 CONT Grandma was certainly old enough to quit working, but the person at the Social Security office told her if she could work one more year, they could raise her Social Security a little more.  So she bought the house on Harold Street
3 CONC , and rented it out until she had it paid for.  She moved into her house September 5, 1957.  She was 70 years old.
