2 TITL Inga teaching Barbara to crochet
2 NOTE I know.  I can look at this and hear Grandma's voice.  She was such a good teacher, and I just loved sitting with her.  I especially loved leaning on her when she told stories.  
3 CONT Not in this picture . . .on the fireplace mantle just above Barbara's head, there was a pretty glass jar full of hard candy.  We would play with blocks on the floor in front of the fireplace for hours, knowing we were not to ask f
3 CONC or any of the candy.  When it was time to leave, coats were on, and we were lined up by the front door, Auntie Jerry would take down the glass candy jar, and stand by the door.  Each of us could take one piece as we left.  
2 NOTE I can just picture this so beautifully in my mind... how Grandma would try to teach us to crochet!  This is a great photo!
