2 TITL Demonstrating her spinning wheel
2 NOTE Early in her childhood at Kaldfarnes, Inga Marie learned to spin.  She writes, "When the children got to school age, we had to sit with our ABC book on a foot stool close to the spinning wheel.  A stick or knitting needle pointed 
3 CONC at the letters made it easier for Mother to follow the reading when she was spinning."
3 CONT One year, after she retired, Inga Marie bought some wool from a farmer.  She washed it, carded it, spun it into yarn, and wove it on her loom into fine wool fabric.  Four yards for each daughter, and a smaller piece for each grand
3 CONC daughter.  
3 CONT In this newspaper picture she showing some Kindergarten children how to spin.  Often children would stop by her house on their way home fom school to watch her work.
