2 TITL Broken leg - 1950
2 NOTE Summer of 1950 and 1951, Inga Marie was assistant to the Cook at Camp Kilowan, a Campfire Girls camp in the mountains west of Corvallis OR.  About her fall she writes:
3 CONT Just three days before my time was up, I came out the screen door with something in both hands.  I stepped too close to the edge of the porch, and fell sideways. I scraped my elbow, and hit my ankle against the root of a stump.  I
3 CONC  could see the bone was too far out.
3 CONT When we got in the car, I asked the (camp) nurse to take me to my daughter's place in Corvallis.  Bernice called her sister Freda, and when her husband got home from work they came and took me to Portland.  The next morning Herb a
3 CONC nd Freda brought me to Providence Hospital, where my son-in-law was the x-ray technician.
3 CONT When we got into the office, the nurse asked me my name and address.  Boy, did I get embarrassed.  I did not have an address to give.  I had my home rented, and I had left camp.  Then I gave them the x-ray man's name, Dr. Melvin L
3 CONC ee.
1 OBJE
