2 TITL Silverton house
2 NOTE The Hanson family home in Silverton Oregon.  Inga and Tom lived and raised their family here for 30 years.  In 1937, the bank bought  the government loan Tom had taken to get through tough times, and took their house and the farm 
3 CONC from them.
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p7/4966/3456/53444836e50da6f8/Silverton_1923_original.jpg?hash=b898b06535e2e15101f4a88a2c2a4f4122ab6eab1ed9d96533dd88f2c61d9033.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Trinity's Sunday School Picnic at Silverton City Park 1923
2 NOTE Inga Marie is holding Freda (back row on the left).  Freda's hand is wrapped from burning it on the stove.
3 CONT Inga Marie writes - One morning when Freda was about one and a half years old, the children had gone off to school and someone had left the wooden rocker close to the stove in the dining room.  Freda got up in to the chair. but ge
3 CONC tting down the chair tipped her closer to the stove.  She laid her hand right on top of it.  I heard a funny noise, so I ran in and grabbed her.  If she had gotten her hand off, she would have burned her face too.
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p7/4966/3456/53444836ebb2fd77/001_original.jpg?hash=1b0c480e9762cf9294950ad28eacb04fef74748a6784f16f72a34dc8ac98faa1.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Anne and Inga childhood friends - 1910
2 NOTE Anne Størkersdtr and Inga grew up together in Kaldfarnes.  In Inga's Story, Grandma calls her Jana.  Anne came to the USA in 1907, and lived with her husband Hilmar Pederson in Petersburg Alaska for many years.  He was a fisherman
3 CONC .
3 CONT The summer of 1951, Inga came to Seattle to visit Anne and Hilmar in their brand new house.  During her visit, she got a job as a cook for a family in the Highlands just north of downtown Seattle.  It's a very nice gated area over
3 CONC looking Puget Sound.  
3 CONT With Anne and Inga in this picture - Margrethe holding Jerdis.  It must be a special occassion, they all have flowers.  
