1 NAME Ane /Johansdatter/ Mangholmstrand
2 GIVN Ane
2 SURN Johansdatter
2 NSFX Mangholmstrand
2 _MARNM Johansdatter
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1821
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1838 konfirmerte paa Mo: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/2570/128
2 CONT ** barn: Ane Johansdatter Mangholmstrand (17aar, f.1821)
2 CONT ** par.: ungk Johan Johansen og pige Elen Petersd.(?)
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 år og på Mangholmstrand (= Reinfjellet) ved dåpen til sønnen Johan Andreas i 1840. Hennes fosterfar var da [https://www.geni.com/people/Jon-Jonsen-Reinfjellet/6000000125365184823 John Johnsen Mangholmstrand].
2 CONT fadderene: Amund Christensen Trethammer, Amund Wilkensen ibid, Johanna Johansd. ibid, ...
2 CONT
2 CONT DISCUSSION: 1838 konfirmasjon indicates her father as Johan Johansen and could therefore well be the same one that is noted as her foster father in 1840 as John Johnson Mangholmstrand.  Her mother is noted as "Elen" and possibly P
2 CONC etersdatter.  Witnesses at that 1840 baptism were mostly from Trethammer, one of which being Amund Wilkensen Trethammer. (seen also there in 1801FT).  He had a younger brother https://www.geni.com/people/Johannes-Wilchensen/600000
2 CONC 0045910291096 who in 1801FT was at Mangholmstrand.  And so, while we don't see Johan Wilkensen as a father in the 1918-1922 timeframe, given the 1840 "foster" father indication of Johan Johansen Mangholmstrand suggests maybe he wa
2 CONC s simply listed as the real father in 1838 konfirmasjon.  Or perhaps the father was Johan Johansen but his father Johan Johansen Mangholmstrand became the foster parent for Ane?  Best perhaps to find out about her mother Elen Pete
2 CONC rsd.(?).
