2 NOTE A great day for the family to gather at 705 Young St, and celebrate Inga Marie on Mother's Day.  
3 CONT Ruth and Billy and Mom and I were all living with Grandma and Grandpa at this time.  Ruth came in January 1945, soon after she had received the official telegram about Uncle Bill's death in the Philippines.  Mom and I had been the
3 CONC re since January 1944.  
3 CONT Four adults and two babies in a small two bedroom house.  Grandma certainly deserved to be celebrated on this special day.  
2 NOTE Dear Cathy, 
3 CONT Thanks for answering my question about photos.  We have a few we thought would be fun to put in.  We love Geni and I go to it nearly every day.  When I do I find the time whizzes by.  I LOVE the old photos and the history of the f
3 CONC amily.  I am an only child as was my father who died when I was 22 years old.  I have tried to trace family back but have not had much luck so having my Hanson family is so dear to me.  Thank you for all your work to make this hap
3 CONC pen.  We are well and so busy but that is good.  Phil and I send our love and hugs.  Ruth
2 NOTE Hi Ruthie,
3 CONT Just go to the photo button at the top of the page and it will run you through how to upload photos.  Don't forget to add pictures of you too--- and the kids, grandkids and great-grandkids.  Isn't it fun to see the old photos that
3 CONC  people have saved all these years?   We are very lucky that our family likes to keep records and photos!   Have you looked back to see how our family traces back to the 900's and even before.  Hope all is well with you and yours.
3 CONC   I'll be looking for photos from you soon.  Love, Cathy
