2 TITL USS Casco inspection on deck - Aleutian Islands Alaska 1943
2 NOTE William and Ruth married February 19, 1943.  In March he became the Executive Officer of the USS Casco, and patroled the Aleutian Islands in Alaska.
3 CONT About the USS Casco - It was a small seaplane tender, built at the Puget Sound Navy Yard, Bremerton, Washington.  Commissioned in December 1941, it moved in May 1942 to the Aleutians.  Duties included surveying the islands, laying
3 CONC  moorings for seaplanes, and providing tender services.  While at anchor in Nazan Bay in August 1942, Casco was torpedoed by the Japanese submarine RO-61.  It was beached to prevent sinking and, after being refloated in September,
3 CONC  underwent battle damage repairs and modifications at Puget Sound.
3 CONT Casco returned to the Aleutians in March 1943 and in May particpated in the recapture of Attu.  It left the Aleutian theater in November 1943.
