2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p7/4966/3456/534448370d99807f/Billy_at_Vanport_1947_original.jpg?hash=247807b98f791df95d953af5cdeb3885189e27b5a31dea06932c4f0f31b40a68.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Billy plays at Vanport 1947
2 NOTE P.S.   Google Vanport City Oregon.  There's a lot of information and pictures.  It is quite an amazing story of survival.
2 NOTE Vanport City was a huge public housing project in the 1940s.  It was located on the Oregon side of the Columbia River, now called Delta Park.  Most of the people who lived there during the war, were families of those working in th
3 CONC e shipyards building US Liberty ships.  
3 CONT On Memorial Day 1948, the Columbia River was running very high with spring run off from the mountains.  There was a dike protecting Vanport City from The Columbia River.  On this day, the river was 15 feet higher than Vanport City
3 CONC , and the dike broke.  Vanport City was gone in the matter of minutes.
3 CONT Ruth and Billy, and Bee and Morrie lived there in 1947.  It was a post war period, and Vanport City was cheap rent for those looking for jobs.  I do not know if they left before the flood.
2 NOTE What a great photo.  Where or what is Vanport?  I can imagine how much Aunt Ruth loved this photo of her little boy.   He was absolutely everything to her.
