1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * www.alaskahistory.org/detail.aspx?ID=150
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * http://obitz.us/obits/Index%2038/notesobit_38_1502.htm
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * Hope Lucille Lowe,
2 CONT
2 CONT 85, died July 16, 2009, at her Anchorage home with loving family at her side after a year-long battle with cancer. A celebration of life will be at 2 p.m. Saturday at Hope's home. For more information, call Inez Nixa at 279-3073. 
2 CONC Hope Lucille Sperstad was born July 28, 1923, in a little white house on Fourth Avenue and A Street in Anchorage. Hope's parents came to Alaska from Norway around the turn of the century and homesteaded a farm that is now Sperstad
2 CONC  Subdivision, near Arctic Boulevard and International Airport Road. She graduated from Anchorage High School in 1941 and attended the University of Washington for four years. There she met her future husband, Robert C. Lowe. Over 
2 CONC the years, she worked for Mannings Restaurant in Seattle and the National Weather Bureau in Anchorage, but her greatest achievements were her children, grandchildren and great-grandchildren. She is survived by her children, Karen 
2 CONC Brian of Juneau, Karl Lowe of Anchorage, Nelson Lowe of Anchorage and Inez Nixa of Eagle River; her ex-husband, Robert C. Lowe; nine grandchildren; four great-grandchildren; and numerous nieces, nephews, neighbors and friends who 
2 CONC also loved her. She was preceded in death by her sister and two brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in adn.com from 7/21 to 7/22/2009
